{
  "answer_text": "The bug is in `helper_b`: it passes `skb + 1` to `helper_c`, which creates a modified ctx pointer with offset 192 (sizeof struct __sk_buff = 192). The BPF verifier disallows dereferencing a ctx pointer that has been offset.\n\nThe fix is to just pass `skb` instead of `skb + 1`:\n\n```c\n__attribute__((noinline))\nint helper_b(int val, struct __sk_buff *skb)\n{\n\treturn helper_a(skb) + helper_c(val, skb);\n}\n```",
